guamp: contiguous-first back-off and wired accounting (NativeAdrenoMemory, NativeAdrenoUserClient; NativeAdreno 81a0b01 + 0001..0006)

fin6b/fin8: vm_page_find_contiguous(num=16384) "found 0 pages", each followed by "zone_gc called" (1038 lines in one boot). A user BO of
64 KiB or more tries one contiguous run first; once memory is fragmented the Metal runtime's 64 MiB blocks never get one, and every
failed attempt costs three scans of all of RAM, a buffer cache flush and a zone trim and drain before the scattered allocation it ends
in anyway. Now:
- after a contiguous failure of N bytes, contiguous-first attempts of N bytes or more are skipped for 15 s (smaller ones still try,
  the first one after the window tries again): the BO is the same scattered one, without the scans;
- native_adreno_bo_mem: live bytes of whole/scattered objects, pooled objects and imported (wired) user ranges, and the contiguous
  attempts tried / got / failed / skipped with the size the back-off holds; GuampDisplayExt.inc logs them.

